{"name":"Mǔ Lì Bái Oyster","hex":"#f1f2d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oyster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of certain marine bivalve mollusks, especially those of the family Ostreidae (the true oysters), usually found adhering to rocks or other fixed objects in shallow water along the seacoasts, or in brackish water in the mouth of rivers.","The delicate oyster-shaped morsel of dark meat contained in a small cavity of the bone on each side of the lower part of the back of a fowl."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale beige colour tinted with grey or pink, like that of an oyster."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oyster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Li Bai","blocks":[{"text":"Li Bai, also known by his courtesy name of Taibai, was a Chinese poet acclaimed as one of the best and most important poets of the Tang dynasty, and even in the whole of Chinese poetry. He and his friends such as Du Fu (712–770) were among the prominent figures in the flourishing of Chinese poetry of the Tang dynasty, often called the \"Golden Age of Chinese Poetry\". The expression \"Three Wonders\" denotes Li Bai's poetry, Pei Min's swordplay, and Zhang Xu's calligraphy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/LiBai.jpg/330px-LiBai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Bai"},{"title":"Bai (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Bái is the pinyin of the surname 白, meaning the colour white."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b8/%E7%99%BD-order.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bai_(surname)"},{"title":"Oyster","blocks":[{"text":"Oyster is the common name for a number of different families of salt-water bivalve molluscs that live in marine or brackish habitats. In some species, the valves are highly calcified, and many are 